
BODY
PART XIV - PENALTIES AND PROCEDURES
	SEC 281.  - Offences and penalties.
		SUBSEC (1)
			Any person who contravenes any provision of this Act or any rule or notification made or issued thereunder or fails to comply with any provision thereof which it was his duty to comply with, shall be liable to penalty or be guilty of an offence under this Act and if in respect of any such contravention or offence no penalty or punishment is specially provided, he shall be liable to penalty which may extend to fifty thousand rupees.
		SUBSEC (2)
			The contraventions mentioned in column (2) of the table below, shall be liable  to  the  extent  of  penalty  mentioned  in  column  (4)  of  the  said  table,  with reference to such contraventions, respectively.
